`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"create-a-progress-tracker",children:"Create a progress tracker"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Build a spreadsheet to log workouts and track improvement over time. Claude can create a structured log with dates, exercises, reps, pain levels, and notes—making it easy to see patterns and share progress with your PT."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(i,{children:(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Create an Excel spreadsheet to track this routine. Include columns for date, each exercise with sets/reps, pain level before and after (1-10 scale), notes about how it felt, and any modifications I made. Add a summary sheet that calculates weekly totals and shows progress trends over time."})}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"learn-the-science-behind-it",children:"Learn the science behind it"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Understand what's actually happening in your knee and why it hurts. Claude can research the biomechanics, explain which structures are involved in your injury, and show how each exercise targets specific problems."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(i,{children:(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Explain the anatomy of patellar tendinitis—what structures are damaged, why do they get inflamed, and what's the mechanical problem causing pain? Then show me how each exercise in this routine addresses a specific part of the issue. I want to understand what I'm fixing, not just follow instructions."})}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"adapt-the-routine-as-you-improve",children:"Adapt the routine as you improve"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Modify exercises when they become too easy or your situation changes. Claude can progress the difficulty, swap exercises that aren't working, or scale back if you're experiencing setbacks."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(i,{children:(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"These exercises are getting easier—I can do the full sets without much effort now. Progress this routine to the next level: harder variations, more resistance, or additional exercises that build on what I've mastered. Keep it appropriate for continuing knee rehab."})}),`
